1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,620
He stole the Mona Lisa, then got caught asking for money.

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:09,940
Let's back up. Paris, nineteen eleven. Vincenzo Peruggia used to work at the Louvre.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:15,180
On a Monday when the museum was closed, he walked out with the Mona Lisa under his arm.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,620
Nobody noticed until the next day, when a painter saw four empty hooks.

5
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,320
Tap the heart if that security makes you nervous.

6
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:28,100
And the Louvre? It shut down for a week, and newspapers around the world printed the empty wall.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,300
People still lined up just to stare at the blank spot.

8
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,400
And for over two years, nobody found it.

9
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,820
Where was it? In his little apartment in Paris.

10
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,900
Then, in nineteen thirteen, he got greedy.

11
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:45,000
He wrote to an art dealer in Florence, offering the Mona Lisa for five hundred thousand lire.

12
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,200
Send this to the friend who'd post the stolen car on Facebook.

13
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:53,240
So what did the dealer do? He brought the Uffizi gallery's director to meet him at his hotel.

14
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:57,760
They checked the painting. It was the real one. So they called the police.

15
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:01,740
Two years of hiding, ruined by one letter he wrote himself.

16
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:04,340
Follow if you love when they catch themselves.

17
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:07,120
His excuse? He said he did it for Italy.

18
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:11,880
A court gave him one year and fifteen days in prison, and he served less than a year.

19
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,840
And the theft made the Mona Lisa the most famous painting on Earth.

20
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:20,500
Stealing the world's most famous painting, for under a year. Fair or not?

